{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310859,"nonce":"5ZbMcAvng0pa3xbF8v8seobhn4k=","title":"Phase 4a INT8 + Q4_K_M runtime + Haxe QTensor binding fully working. Root cause of the silent SIGILL was a single missing function-call ...","message":"Resolved 2026-05-19. The Phase 4 Haxe surface now works end-to-end. Detailed write-up below.\n\n\n`/tmp/test_qtensor.hx` (Haxe) produces correct values across the full pipeline:\n\n- `QTensor.fromFloat32(t, INT8)` quantises a Tensor.\n- `qt.rows()`, `qt.cols()`, `qt.numel()`, `qt.scheme()` all return correct properties.\n- `qt.dequant()` produces values within int8 quantisation tolerance\n  (`1.0` round-trips as `1.0078740` — within ulp of int8/127).\n- `qt.matmulF32(b)` produces results within 0.16% of the f32 reference.\n- regression suite at parity 122/128.\n\n\nThe `build_qtensor_types` function in `compiler/src/stdlib/mod.rs` was\nregistered in `build_stdlib()` but **not** in `build_stdlib_with_plugins()`.\nThe compiler only ever invokes `build_stdlib_with_plugins` (the no-plugins\npath is dead code under normal use), so the QTensor MIR wrappers never got\ninto the stdlib module. When user code called `QTensor.fromFloat32(...)`,\nthe dispatcher correctly resolved the runtime mapping to `QTensor_fromFloat32`\nand emitted a `build_call_direct` to it via `register_stdlib_mir_forward_ref` —\nbut the forward reference never got resolved because the actual function\nwasn't in the merged module. The JIT ended up calling into uninitialised\nmemory, producing a silent exit (no error, no crash) once it ran off\nthe end of the empty function body.\n\nOne-line fix: added `qtensor::build_qtensor_types(\u0026mut builder);` to\n`build_stdlib_with_plugins` at compiler/src/stdlib/mod.rs alongside the\nexisting call in `build_stdlib`.\n\n\nWhile diagnosing, I also fixed an unrelated hardcoded `class_name == \"Tensor\"`\nmapping in `detect_stdlib_class_from_call` (hir_to_mir.rs ~line 5212).\nThat function tracks the canonical runtime class name of static factory\ncalls (for `monomorphized_var_types`). Pre-fix it had a one-class special\ncase that worked for Tensor by accident — every other stdlib class\nhappened to have its simple name equal to its mapping key. QTensor (whose\nkey is `rayzor_ds_QTensor`, not the bare `QTensor`) needed a new branch.\n\nThe fix: replaced the hardcoded branch with a generic\n`canonical_stdlib_class_name(symbol)` helper that derives the runtime\nclass name from `symbol.native_name` (`\"rayzor::ds::QTensor\"` →\n`\"rayzor_ds_QTensor\"`) — the same lookup pattern already used by\n`is_stdlib_class_by_symbol`. Future stdlib classes following the\nstandard `@:native(\"a::b::C\")` convention now flow through automatically.\n\nAlso extended the `returns_same_class` allowlist (init / clone / new /\nzeros / ones / full / fromArray / rand) to include `fromFloat32` and\n`wrapQ4KM` — the QTensor factory methods.\n\n\n- /tmp/test_qtensor.hx — full INT8 round-trip + matmul, all values correct.\n- run_haxe_tests.sh — 122/128 parity (unchanged from before).\n- cargo run --release -p compiler --example test_rayzor_stdlib_e2e — 12/12 pass.\n- cargo clippy --release -p rayzor-runtime -- -D warnings — clean.\n\n\nWhen adding a new stdlib class, **two** registration points need updating\nin compiler/src/stdlib/mod.rs:\n  1. `build_stdlib()` — the no-plugins variant (rarely exercised).\n  2. `build_stdlib_with_plugins()` — the actual variant used in normal\n     compilation (called from compilation.rs:4466).\n\nBoth must add the new `xxx::build_xxx_types(\u0026mut builder)` call.\nA missed registration manifests as a silent exit on first call into the\nclass's methods — no error, no diagnostic, just a clean program-exit\nbefore the next user statement. Easy to miss; worth a routine grep for\nnew `build_*_types` calls landing in only one of the two functions.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_quant_haxe_wip` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}